[:option {:value "19019713"} "50 kilometres (Mass Start, Freestyle), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "19019714"} "30 kilometres Skiathlon, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "19019715"} "4 × 10 kilometres Relay, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "19019716"} "Team Sprint (Classical), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "19019721"} "Sprint (Freestyle), Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "19019733"} "10 kilometres (Classical), Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "19019734"} "30 kilometres (Mass Start, Freestyle), Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "19019735"} "15 kilometres Skiathlon, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "19019736"} "4 × 5 kilometres Relay, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "19019737"} "Team Sprint (Classical), Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "2092"} "2002"] "\n" [:option {:value "2135"} "2006"] "\n" [:option {:value "923555"} "2010"] "\n" [:option {:value "350054"} "2014"] "\n" [:option {:value "9000265"} "2018"] "\n" [:option {:value "15000120"} "2026"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/182"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Sprint (Freestyle), Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} " 8 February 2022"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2138"} "Zhangjiakou Nordic Centre and Biathlon Centre, Chongli District, Zhangjiakou City, Hebei Province"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/19019700"} "88 from 44 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Final standings based on time achieved in last round competed in."]] [:tr {} [:th {:valign "top"} "Details"] [:td {} "Course Length: 1,381 m" [:br {}] "Height Differential: 27 m" [:br {}] "Maximum Climb: 25 m" [:br {}] "Total Climbing: 53 m"]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "After the classical style in 2018, the sprint was now run in the freestyle technique. On the demanding course, which was 80 meters longer than in PyeongChang, the Norwegian " [:a {:href "/athletes/137724"} "Johannes Høsflot Klæbo"] " repeated his victory from four years ago. The top favorite prevailed against the Italian " [:a {:href "/athletes/127933"} "Federico Pellegrino"] ", who also won his second consecutive silver. Bronze went to Russian athlete " [:a {:href "/athletes/148780"} "Aleksandr Terentyev"] ". Another of the favorites, 2018 bronze medalist " [:a {:href "/athletes/137797"} "Aleksandr Bolshunov"] ", skipped the race in order to concentrate on the longer events."] "\n\n" [:p {} "For top star Klæbo, who had suffered a bitter defeat in the skiathlon with a 40th place, it was the fourth gold medal of his career. He also became the first runner to win consecutive Olympic sprint titles."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The fastest skier in qualification was " [:a {:href "/athletes/137174"} "Lucas Chanavat"] " from France, who was later eliminated in the semi-final. Both, Pellegrino and Klæbo, won their quarter-finals and qualified 1-2 in the same semi-final. Terentyev finished first in the second semi-final. The other three finalists were " [:a {:href "/athletes/148283"} "Joni Mäki"] " (Finland), " [:a {:href "/athletes/148778"} "Artyom Maltsev"] " (ROC), and " [:a {:href "/athletes/138162"} "Oskar Svensson"] " (Sweden)."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Klæbo and Pellegrino controlled the field from the start. After the last climb, only the three eventual medalists were still together. But on the home stretch, the third placed Terentyev had no chance to catch the leading two. On the final run-in, it was just Klæbo and Pellegrino, with Klæbo outpacing the Italian by 0.26."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table tabl